cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use partial-recall in academic work, please cite it using
  the metadata below.
title: "partial-recall"
abstract: >-
  Semantic memory for a scholar's corpus. Local-first, offline-capable
  vector search over Zotero libraries and directories of documents,
  with full-text (FTS5) keyword fallback and an MCP server interface
  for use from Claude Code and other MCP-compatible clients. Designed
  for marginalised scholars on low-power machines (4–8 GB RAM),
  CPU-only, with no required API key or institutional subscription.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Commoner LLP"
    affiliation: "CommonerLLP"
repository-code: "https://github.com/CommonerLLP/partial-recall"
url: "https://github.com/CommonerLLP/partial-recall"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - semantic search
  - vector embeddings
  - Zotero
  - digital humanities
  - South Asian studies
  - multilingual
  - local-first
  - MCP
  - Model Context Protocol
